  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The basic square uses "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "double-crochet-uk"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "double crochet"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " throughout instead of treble clusters, giving a denser, flatter fabric than the granny square — well suited to pot holders, bag panels, and blankets that need structure. The "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "chain-2-corner"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "chain-2 corner"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " at each of the four corners is what keeps the square shape: two chains give the fabric enough angle to turn 90 degrees without buckling. Each round adds 8 stitches to the total count — 2 per side. Start with a "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "magic-ring"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "magic ring"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " to close the centre completely."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "infoPanel",
        "attrs": {
          "type": "materials"
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Yarn: DK cotton, approx 20 m per square. Hook: 4 mm. Notions: tapestry needle, scissors."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Gauge"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "10 × 10 cm in DK cotton on a 4 mm hook, steam-blocked. The dc fabric is denser than a treble-based square so gauge is critical for blanket planning."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Stitches used"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Magic ring"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Chain (ch)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Double crochet (dc) — UK: short upright stitch"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Slip stitch (sl st)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pattern"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 1"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Make a magic ring. Ch 2, work 2 dc into the ring. *(Ch 2, 3 dc into ring); repeat from * 2 more times. Ch 2. Sl st to top of first dc to join. Pull the tail to close the ring. (12 dc, 4 ch-2 corner sps)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 2"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sl st into corner sp. Ch 1, (2 dc, ch 2, 2 dc) into corner sp. *1 dc in each st across side, (2 dc, ch 2, 2 dc) in corner sp; repeat from * 2 more times. 1 dc in each remaining st. Sl st to first dc to join. (20 dc, 4 ch-2 corner sps)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 3"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sl st into corner sp. Ch 1, (2 dc, ch 2, 2 dc) into corner sp. *1 dc in each st across side, (2 dc, ch 2, 2 dc) in corner sp; repeat from * 2 more times. 1 dc in each remaining st. Sl st to first dc to join. (28 dc, 4 ch-2 corner sps)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 4"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sl st into corner sp. Ch 1, (2 dc, ch 2, 2 dc) into corner sp. *1 dc in each st across side, (2 dc, ch 2, 2 dc) in corner sp; repeat from * 2 more times. 1 dc in each remaining st. Sl st to first dc to join. Fasten off. (36 dc, 4 ch-2 corner sps)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Chart"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "craftChart",
        "attrs": {
          "roundCount": 4
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Finishing"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Weave in both ends using a tapestry needle. Steam-block: hold a steam iron 1 cm above the square and apply steam, then press with a damp cloth to sharpen corners. Pin to 10 × 10 cm while damp and leave to dry."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Joining"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Join squares using the flat slip-stitch join: place two squares with right sides together, insert hook through both corner spaces, and slip stitch along the edge through corresponding dc pairs. At each corner chain-2 space, work 1 sl st into the space itself to maintain the corner angle."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Care"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Machine wash at 40 degrees. Reshape while damp and dry flat. The dc fabric is dense enough to hold shape without re-blocking after each wash."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What to try next"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "To add a fifth round, follow the same pattern: sl st to corner sp, (2 dc, ch 2, 2 dc) in each corner, 1 dc in every side stitch between. The total will reach 44 dc at round 5 (approx 12.5 cm). For a colour-blocked version, change colour at the start of each round by fastening off and rejoining."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}